<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mekong River</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mekong</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mekong is a major river of South-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-asia">East Asia</a>, flowing from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a> through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/laos">Laos</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambodia">Cambodia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>. Its basin and floodplains supported <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> agriculture and early states. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-empire">Khmer Empire</a> was founded by uniting polities of the Mekong basin into a centralised state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mekong-river.jpg" alt="Mekong River" width="320" height="221" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bjørn Christian Tørrissen · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mekong-River-Near-Luang-Prabang.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
